## Shared Web implementation checkpoint ΓÇö exact Portfolio v1 payload binding

Shared Web has now materialized a fail-closed Web adapter for the exact public v1 payload semantics supplied by Application commit `b922ef446dd0b99257acddfedfe81193ac1489fb`.

Implemented/reconciled:
- exact `{brokerId, brokerAccountId, environment}` scope validation;
- exact contract identity/version checks;
- exact `truthState`, `freshnessState`, `completeness`, `availabilityState` semantics;
- null numeric values preserved; no zero-fill;
- exact order lifecycle includes `PARTIALLY_FILLED`, `CANCELLED`, `UNKNOWN_BROKER_OUTCOME` and is never collapsed to `FILLED`;
- previous hard-coded UI `FILLED` state removed;
- previous hard-coded `+2.35%` / `+21.74%` portfolio/dashboard performance values removed;
- presenters consume Application envelope, `order.value`, `instrument.value`, truth/freshness/reason/effective-time fields.

Evidence includes:
- `src/adapters/fsats-portfolio-v1.js` @ `80e4cfdad3cbf4948ba6e31194fa077d8b491274`;
- `src/presenters.js` @ `549d69ddaeef21f65f64c716cdc9c101c7b0a403`;
- portfolio/activity/dashboard corrections at `9f59b71f549f0722da10f082774528ed1a38f711`, `45c99c22c9c2773aa2809623d2cb5aa10af1bf89`, `5d49df0b2e88488017b41ca46fcdeaa9cbeadcaa`;
- focused contract tests at `05b6d72bbad82c7daf12c0aff08712799f52e84c` and subsequent presentation tests.

The Application contract explicitly states no executable public transport route is materialized/authorized. Shared Web therefore does not invent a route. Payload binding is implemented; executable transport/runtime binding remains a governed future step.

Checkpoint: `applications/shared/web/docs/FCR_RECONCILIATION_IMPLEMENTATION_CHECKPOINT_03.md` @ `757c7d48fcda17b5b8dbfb886765fe71b1467273`.

No closure is claimed because full governed executable Web verification and the executable public runtime route remain pending.

